<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:22:39 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Israel a rare dissenting voice as praise pours in for Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-israel-a-rare-dissenting-voice-as-praise-pours-in-for-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay</link><description>
Advocates of human rights and international justice cheered, even as Israeli officials fumed, after South African jurist and former UN human rights chief Navi Pillay won the Nobel Peace Prize on Friday. The 85-year-old drew wide praise for decades of work, including investigating crimes in Rwanda, Israel and the occupied Palestinian territories. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4cee3a6e-c3c9-11f1-bbfc-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T091255Z-1569360422-RC2LZNAVP694-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4cee3a6e-c3c9-11f1-bbfc-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T091255Z-1569360422-RC2LZNAVP694-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3aefb3ca-c3f0-11f1-8c9b-8399f5a7519d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:20:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4cee3a6e-c3c9-11f1-bbfc-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T091255Z-1569360422-RC2LZNAVP694-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg">© Valentin Flauraud, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Falling test scores in schools startle EU countries: Why are standards going down?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-falling-test-scores-in-schools-startle-eu-countries-why-are-standards-going-down</link><description>
It has been dubbed "the PISA shock". Countries that had been used to their school pupils performing well in test scores are seeing a plunge in standards. The PISA test is an international assessment led by the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), which measures how well 15‑year‑olds in over 80 countries apply reading, mathematics and science skills to real‑world problems. In the latest rankings, France's results were the worst it has ever had, and Germany's school pupils got their worst PISA report card too.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/602dd6fc-c15d-11f1-9e8b-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/Debate-Pisa2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/602dd6fc-c15d-11f1-9e8b-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/Debate-Pisa2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e07f6244-c15d-11f1-915e-c1ae4f7ce44b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:03:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Scoop</category><title>Lawsuits blame Fox News for deaths of journalists in Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261009-lawsuits-blame-fox-news-for-deaths-of-journalists-in-ukraine</link><description>
This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop revisits a fatal assignment for a Fox News team in Ukraine. On March 14, 2022, a Russian strike hit the crew reporting near the capital Kyiv. Reporter Benjamin Hall was seriously injured and two other journalists were killed. The journalists' families are suing Fox, saying the network put the story ahead of its people. Our guest is NPR's David Folkenflik.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/df088b96-c3df-11f1-9db5-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16543625836ac8e2dae116b5-18744395.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/df088b96-c3df-11f1-9db5-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16543625836ac8e2dae116b5-18744395.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21d41366-c3de-11f1-8f1a-ff81f5596910</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:23:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>William HILDERBRANDT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Residents of Ukraine's Kramatorsk forced to flee as drone strikes intensify</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261009-residents-of-ukraine-s-kramatorsk-forced-to-flee-as-drone-strikes-intensify</link><description>
The city of Kramatorsk, in eastern Ukraine, is increasingly coming under Russian attack. For those who have stayed behind, the threat from drones and shelling has become a daily reality. Many have resisted leaving their homes, despite the growing danger – but now, more and more residents are being forced to flee. Our colleagues at France 2 followed an evacuation from the city and witnessed first-hand the dangers that residents face.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a254ec88-c3d7-11f1-a4ce-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14410476136ac8d50910b737-10104573.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a254ec88-c3d7-11f1-a4ce-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14410476136ac8d50910b737-10104573.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b0984d42-c32f-11f1-937c-813a6b8358d6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:51:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 2</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>South Africa's Navi Pillay wins 2026 Nobel Peace Prize</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-south-africa-s-navanethem-navi-pillay-wins-2026-nobel-peace-prize</link><description>
Former UN human rights chief and International Court of Justice judge Navanethem "Navi" Pillay has won the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize for her contributions to international law, the Nobel jury announced on Friday. The Nobel committee denied it was taking a stance on whether Israel is committing genocide in Gaza by awarding Pillay, who led a UN inquiry on the subject, after Israel said honouring her legitimised "anti-Israel hatred".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/879b9b0a-c3c1-11f1-8bec-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/000-337M979.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/879b9b0a-c3c1-11f1-8bec-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/000-337M979.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b46e72a-c3b9-11f1-a8b1-759d170e0a5b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 09:03:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/879b9b0a-c3c1-11f1-8bec-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/000-337M979.jpg">© Wikus de Wet, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French student protests: Police impunity ‘below' the standards of a 'well-functioning democracy’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-french-student-protests-police-impunity-below-the-standards-of-a-well-functioning-democracy-1</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Dr. Antoine Marie, postdoctoral researcher, fellow and lecturer at Sciences Po / CEVIPOF, to explore the political psychology behind France’s student protests. Why do people witness the same events yet reach radically different conclusions about violence? Dr Marie examines how media echo chambers, partisan thinking and the politicization of empathy deepen polarization, making it easier to overlook the suffering of those perceived as political opponents. He also examines France’s increasingly offensive police doctrine, questions surrounding accountability, and the institutional incentives that may actually hinder independent investigations into police misconduct.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/977a2c78-c347-11f1-a553-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-151311-152324-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/977a2c78-c347-11f1-a553-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-151311-152324-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8feee3e-c347-11f1-bc8e-5ff5dfc17852</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 06:55:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Tens of thousands march in Madrid to mourn pensioner whose eviction sparked housing protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-tens-of-thousands-march-in-madrid-to-mourn-pensioner-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests</link><description>
Tens of thousands of protesters joined a march in Madrid Thursday to mark the death of 87-year-old retiree Maricarmen Abascal, whose eviction from her apartment in the Spanish capital in September sparked a wave of housing protests that prompted the government to call early elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/56551082-c3ab-11f1-902b-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T183913Z-944686721-RC26ZNABD0G8-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-MARICARMEN-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/56551082-c3ab-11f1-902b-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T183913Z-944686721-RC26ZNABD0G8-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-MARICARMEN-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">976b23ec-c3a9-11f1-a540-8d0d67d73d24</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 06:45:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/56551082-c3ab-11f1-902b-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T183913Z-944686721-RC26ZNABD0G8-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-MARICARMEN-PROTEST.jpg">© Violeta Santos Moura, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump envoys, European officials to discuss ‘new ideas’ for Ukraine peace in Miami</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-trump-envoys-ukraine-peace-talks-miami</link><description>
US President Donald Trump’s envoys will meet Ukrainian negotiators and European officials in Miami on Friday to discuss a new proposal to end Russia’s war in Ukraine. Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will present ideas developed during recent talks with both sides, one source said Thursday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/522e42a4-aa19-11f1-b141-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T161535Z-722947549-RC2SDNAERMLR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-ENVOYS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/522e42a4-aa19-11f1-b141-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T161535Z-722947549-RC2SDNAERMLR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-ENVOYS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad372da8-c35c-11f1-a196-5577fbbf20aa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:19:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/522e42a4-aa19-11f1-b141-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T161535Z-722947549-RC2SDNAERMLR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-ENVOYS.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Black Sea and black ops: How exposed is Europe to Ukraine war spillover?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261008-black-sea-and-black-ops-how-exposed-is-europe-to-ukraine-war-spillover</link><description>
The story is as underreported as it is consequential for the entire planet. Three Turkish-owned cargo ships out of Ukraine have been hit in EU waters by suspected Russian drones. One, the Togo-flagged Alfa Watan, sunk on Tuesday off Bulgaria. Ten Egyptian and Syrian crew members are missing. For its part, Ukraine has been hitting Russian tankers in the Black Sea, with no sign of a return to a UN-brokered deal to allow oil, grain and fertiliser ships to pass. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4d9528e-c342-11f1-b42c-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T155502Z-91069183-RC2XYNAVY1S2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4d9528e-c342-11f1-b42c-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T155502Z-91069183-RC2XYNAVY1S2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-REGION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb14136c-c341-11f1-913a-1f7dde354c7d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 20:42:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain mourns Maricarmen Abascal, whose eviction sparked housing protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-mourns-maricarmen-abascal-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests</link><description>
Protests and anger have grown across Spain after the death of an 87-year-old woman in the wake of her eviction from her home. Maricarmen Abascal was thrown out of her home of seven decades in what became the "cause celebre" of Spain's housing crisis. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16c7f1bc-c353-11f1-8507-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-201454-202032-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16c7f1bc-c353-11f1-8507-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-201454-202032-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c0d8c86-c353-11f1-9a33-ad271529dc2c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 20:35:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Two Latvian men arrested at UK base housing US and NATO intelligence hubs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-two-latvian-men-arrested-at-uk-base-housing-us-and-nato-intelligence-hubs</link><description>
British ​counter-terrorism police are investigating after two Latvian men were arrested Thursday near a Royal Air Force ​base in southeast England housing US and NATO intelligence operations, police said in a statement. The arrests come days after a major incident at another UK base led the US military to withdraw B-1 bombers stationed there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6623278a-c336-11f1-bdb0-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T162911Z-1517542276-RC24ZNAZJCYB-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SECURITY-MOLESWORTH.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6623278a-c336-11f1-bdb0-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T162911Z-1517542276-RC24ZNAZJCYB-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SECURITY-MOLESWORTH.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1dd8a91a-c335-11f1-9eb9-01fc260ba49b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:57:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6623278a-c336-11f1-bdb0-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T162911Z-1517542276-RC24ZNAZJCYB-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SECURITY-MOLESWORTH.jpg">© Chris Radburn, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>French, US and Russian astronauts return to Earth after eight months in space</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-french-us-and-russian-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space</link><description>
SpaceX brought France's Sophie Adenot and fellow astronauts Jessica Meir, Jack Hathaway and Andrey Fedyaev back to Earth on Thursday after an eight-month mission on board the International Space Station that saw Adenot become the first French woman to walk in space.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edba0678-c2f0-11f1-bba7-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279503330492.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edba0678-c2f0-11f1-bba7-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279503330492.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">302abbda-c330-11f1-930b-734e0890a6e7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:02:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edba0678-c2f0-11f1-bba7-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279503330492.jpg">© Anil Menon, NASA via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Search warrants for former prince Andrew's homes were unlawful, UK court rules</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules</link><description>
Police who searched the properties of Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor as part of investigations into his links to the late sex offender Jeffrey Epstein have agreed the search warrants were unlawful, a London judge said Thursday. The 66-year-old younger brother of King Charles II was arrested on February 19 on suspicion of misconduct in public office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec3669a6-c320-11f1-9c1d-5564e18e22be</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:09:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg">©  Kirsty Wigglesworth, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>New Paris exhibition explores Ireland's housing crisis through contemporary art</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art</link><description>
Huge demonstrations have been held over the last few weeks in Spain over its housing crisis, but the issue is not restricted to Spain. Many other countries also have a huge problem with housing, including Ireland, with experts saying that for every street of 10 houses, the country actually needs 12. Now a new exhibition in Paris at the Irish Cultural Centre is trying to reflect the issue. In Perspective, we spoke to the museum's director and one of the artists taking part.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477d6478-c31b-11f1-a419-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13830491366ac7990734e0d4-77560906.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477d6478-c31b-11f1-a419-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13830491366ac7990734e0d4-77560906.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5640a08e-c315-11f1-8972-1196b899eff1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:29:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Maricarmen, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction shook Spain, dies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-maricarmen-the-87-year-old-woman-whose-eviction-shook-spain-dies</link><description>
María del Carmen Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction from her longtime Madrid home sparked nationwide protests across Spain and unleashed a political crisis, died on Wednesday while hospitalised.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b2a060-c30b-11f1-915d-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-35.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b2a060-c30b-11f1-915d-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-35.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6faf851c-c30b-11f1-a865-3f79da3b2fc9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:54:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Nobel Prize in Literature awarded to Canada’s Anne Carson</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson</link><description>
The Nobel Prize in Literature was awarded to Canadian poet and essayist Anne Carson on Thursday by the Swedish Academy in Stockholm. Toronto-born Carson, 76, draws from ancient Greek and Roman literature for her works blending elements of poetry, essay and fiction. She will receive 12 million Swedish kronor (about $1.2 million) alongside the prestigious award.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8550d60-c2f6-11f1-8765-cfeb110a5623</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:04:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg">©  Andy Kropa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen, symbol of Spain's housing crisis, dies at 87</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261008-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-symbol-of-spain-s-housing-crisis-dies-at-87</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 8: Maricarmen, the evicted Spanish pensioner who became the face of Spain's housing crisis, dies in hospital. Also, France braces for "Act Four" of high school student protests against dilapidated schools and poor staff presence. Finally, actress Zendaya sparks a row over etiquette at Paris Fashion Week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558cc210-c2e0-11f1-8bbe-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-08T05-20-42-110Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558cc210-c2e0-11f1-8bbe-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-08T05-20-42-110Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a9ddac8-c2e0-11f1-89c2-ed80457c6312</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:35:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>More than 30 killed in Russian strike on buses in Ukraine's Kramatorsk as Kyiv targets data centre</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-russian-strike-buses-kills-at-least-12-ukraine-kramatorsk-kyiv-targets-data-centre</link><description>
