Assassinated Russian journalist Anna Politkovskaya "predicted" Moscow's trajectory under President Vladimir Putin 20 years ago,  her former editor said ahead of the anniversary of her death on Wednesday. Politkovskaya had reported on the war in Chechnya and Putin's rise before she was gunned down in her Moscow apartment block on October 7, 2006.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f785f036-c223-11f1-acd5-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23318667254630.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f785f036-c223-11f1-acd5-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23318667254630.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0921dc0-c223-11f1-ab67-95927788547b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 08:32:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f785f036-c223-11f1-acd5-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23318667254630.jpg">© Pavel Golovkin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia launches one of its biggest strikes on Ukraine, killing at least 21 civilians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-at-least-two-killed-in-fire-caused-by-massive-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
Russian missiles and drones killed at least 21 people in Ukraine, including four children, in what President Volodymyr Zelensky ‌called a “massive” strike on Wednesday. Ukraine has come under increased attack in recent weeks as Russian attacks have targeted energy infrastructure and rail and road transport.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bc7294e-c211-11f1-8aec-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T053758Z-164245437-RC22YNA4P69K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bc7294e-c211-11f1-8aec-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T053758Z-164245437-RC22YNA4P69K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b4a2f570-c20f-11f1-be00-9d3dece0adb8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 05:56:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bc7294e-c211-11f1-8aec-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T053758Z-164245437-RC22YNA4P69K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Vladyslav Sodel, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump says will speak with Putin over Russia's reported plague death</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-trump-says-he-will-speak-to-putin-over-reported-plague-death-in-russia</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Tuesday he would speak “very soon” with Russian President Vladimir Putin over the reported death from plague of a laboratory technician, as Washington and the World Health Organization pressed Moscow for greater transparency and clarity over conflicting accounts of the incident in Siberia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35f3ab30-c16e-11f1-8701-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/0d9752045f8fa082683fe0099656b7298c90813f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35f3ab30-c16e-11f1-8701-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/0d9752045f8fa082683fe0099656b7298c90813f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83da361a-c1d8-11f1-aee6-5f1a754fd3d8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 22:51:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35f3ab30-c16e-11f1-8701-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/0d9752045f8fa082683fe0099656b7298c90813f.jpg">© Igor Ivanko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany's former spy chief detained on suspicion of trading state secrets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-former-german-spy-chief-detained-over-suspected-treasonous-espionage</link><description>
Former German spy chief August Hanning was detained Tuesday on suspicion of treason and espionage after prosecutors accused him of paying for secret intelligence documents and using them to prepare an analysis for a foreign intelligence service, in a case that could strain Berlin’s ties with allied spy agencies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95531a82-c189-11f1-8815-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/91a7ef13c7a16e3d52ad91fa615eb093b8a68a0f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95531a82-c189-11f1-8815-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/91a7ef13c7a16e3d52ad91fa615eb093b8a68a0f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6a68898-c1cd-11f1-886a-5fc42d75ec39</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 21:34:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95531a82-c189-11f1-8815-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/91a7ef13c7a16e3d52ad91fa615eb093b8a68a0f.jpg">© Abdelhak Senna, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Russian lab worker's death sparks plague fears as unverified claims spread online</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261006-russian-lab-worker-s-death-sparks-plague-fears-as-unverified-claims-spread-online-1</link><description>
The death of a 28-year-old Russian lab worker at Siberia's Irkutsk Anti-Plague Research Institute has sparked online panic about a "plague, despite the WHO assessing the public health risk in Russia as low. Unverified claims about how the worker became ill, including a laboratory accident involving a test tube, are circulating online. Misleading posts and out-of-context videos have also fuelled speculation and fear. Vedika Bahl goes through them, and what we know, in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45f2fbf0-c1c6-11f1-be56-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12002312286ac55cea366708-19046261.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45f2fbf0-c1c6-11f1-be56-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12002312286ac55cea366708-19046261.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc75c5fc-c1c5-11f1-bd68-fb988e5cfdc5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 20:58:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Police make seventh arrest over UK airbase incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident</link><description>
A seventh man was arrested Tuesday over a major incident last month at a British military airbase used by the United States to launch strikes on Iran, police said. The arrest came a day after President Donald Trump said the United States had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from RAF Fairford because of "threats" he believed were linked to Tehran. A 22-year-old British male was arrested in London "on suspicion of preparation of terrorist acts", Britain's Counter-Terrorism Policing network said in a statement. Six men in their 20s have already been arrested and released on bail after three suspicious vans were stopped near the base in southwest England on September 27. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0355f7dc-c1be-11f1-9453-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-203840-204355-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0355f7dc-c1be-11f1-9453-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-203840-204355-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0872f008-c1be-11f1-902a-15b8d05e51cb</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:51:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>German ex-spy chief arrested for suspected espionage, treason</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason</link><description>
A former German spy chief was arrested Tuesday on suspicion of espionage and treason, an embarrassing case at a time when the country is seeking to broaden the powers of its intelligence agencies. August Hanning, who ran Germany's BND foreign intelligence agency from 1998 to 2005, is accused of espionage, treason and working for foreign intelligence services, federal prosecutors said. FRANCE 24's Nick Holdsworth reports from Berlin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a786f758-c1bd-11f1-b53b-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-204356-204757-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a786f758-c1bd-11f1-b53b-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-204356-204757-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ada39420-c1bd-11f1-9396-37dc3b8a76ed</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:42:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
